    "message": "fix: read AKS OIDC issuer from live cluster (drift fix)\n\nThe federated identity credential's `issuer` was pinned via\n`var.cluster_oidc_issuer_url` with a hardcoded default. When\ninfra-bootstrap rebuilt the AKS cluster, the cluster's `oidc_issuer_url`\nchanged but this variable kept its old value, so the pod's projected SA\ntoken (signed by the new issuer) failed to match Azure's stored\nfederated credential and the SDK crashed with AADSTS700211 —\nCrashLoopBackOff at startup, 503 at the edge.\n\nSwitch to `data.azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.infra.oidc_issuer_url` so the\ncredential is always pinned to whatever the cluster reports today.\nMatches diagrams/tofu/identity.tf (and every other healthy app UAMI).\n\nDrop the now-unused `cluster_oidc_issuer_url` variable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
